{% doc %}
  Shortens a size to its code.

  Option values are often written out in full — "Small (S)", "Medium (M)" — which
  is right for the cart and the order confirmation but far too long for a chip.
  Where a short form is given in brackets, that is what gets shown; anything
  without brackets is passed through untouched, so "XL" and "2XL" are safe.

  Kept in one place so the shop filters, the featured jersey and the product page
  can never disagree about how a size is written.

  @param {string} label - The full option value.

  @example
  {% render 'brand-size-label', label: value.label %}
{% enddoc %}

{{- label | split: '(' | last | remove: ')' | strip -}}
